A17 applies NOTHING from the shared external-v4l2_codec2 series — see SKIP.

This directory OVERRIDES the shared one wholesale (see patchAppliesTo and the apply loop in
core/SourcePatches.cpp: <dir>-a<N> wins when it exists), so whatever is here is exactly what A17
gets. Nothing is lost by skipping: 0001-0004 are already present on A17, every hunk of them, in
the container-patch commit "A17: Remora c2-va enablement for the VAAPI Codec2 path"
(container-patches/android-17.0.0/external/v4l2_codec2/0001), and 0005 (FLAG_DROP_FRAME on
kAborted) is carried for A17 by 0003 of that same container-patch series. Details in SKIP.

HISTORY, because this directory has been through both failure modes (bd remora-22n):

 1. A blanket SKIP silently swallowed a later patch that A17 did need — the one adding
    VideoCodec::AV1 to the shared codec enum. It landed in this series after the SKIP was
    verified, so every A17 source build from then on died with "no member named 'AV1' in
    'android::VideoCodec'" until the enum patch was made to apply on A17.
 2. The first fix listed that one patch alone here instead — but the apply loop looks for the
    REGISTRY's filenames in the resolved dir, so every build emitted four expected "error: can't
    open patch" lines for 0001-0004. Errors that are routine noise are exactly what hid failure
    mode 1.

THE RESOLUTION: the AV1 enum patch is its own registry entry now (v4l2_av1_enum,
external-v4l2_codec2-av1/), scoped to every version, out of reach of this SKIP. A change A17
needs goes in its own entry or in the A17 container-patch series — never into this shared
series on the assumption that A17 will pick it up.
